// Minimal: the VSCode base keymap does the work, this adds only the three
// test tasks.
//
// One chord root rather than three flat keys. cmd-alt-t is free in both
// Zed's default-macos and VSCode keymaps; cmd-alt-l and cmd-alt-a are not —
// they are already agent::ManageSkills and agent::OpenPermissionDropdown.
//
//   cmd-alt-t f   file
//   cmd-alt-t l   line under the cursor
//   cmd-alt-t a   all
[
  {
    "context": "Workspace",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-alt-t f": ["task::Spawn", { "task_name": "ruby: test file" }],
      "cmd-alt-t l": ["task::Spawn", { "task_name": "ruby: test at cursor" }],
      "cmd-alt-t a": ["task::Spawn", { "task_name": "ruby: full suite" }]
    }
  }
]
